  "name": "Parranda de San Pedro (Guarenas and Guatire)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "The Parranda de San Pedro is the 29 June devotion to Saint Peter in Guarenas and Guatire, Miranda state, which re-enacts the story of the enslaved woman María Ignacia, whose daughter the saint healed. Parranderos in frock coats and top hats sing to the saint with cuatro and maracas while the dancers strike the ground with cotizas, pieces of hard leather strapped to their feet; UNESCO inscribed it in 2013. The foot-stomp card stands in for the cotizas.",
